for(const t of [...new Set(past.map(q=>q.topic))].sort()){const qs=past.filter(q=>q.topic===t);analysis+=`| ${t} | ${qs.length} | ${new Set(qs.map(q=>`${q.provenance.paper}-${q.provenance.question.match(/^\d+/)[0]}`)).size} | ${new Set(qs.map(q=>q.provenance.paper)).size} | ${qs.reduce((s,q)=>s+q.marks,0)} |\n`;}
analysis+='\n## Professor mapping and study priority\n\n| Priority | Topic group | Evidence / preparation target |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Core | Truth tables | P3 Q1; P5 Q1. Fill every row and intermediate column; compare full statements. |\n| Core | Induction | P2 Q2; P3 Q3; P4 Q6; P5 Q2. Basis, hypothesis, justified step, quantified conclusion. |\n| Core | Relations / equivalence classes | Not a standalone question in these papers; explicitly prioritised by the professor. Do not infer low importance from zero past frequency. |\n| Core | POSET / bounds / lattices | P2 Q3; P3 Q4; P4 Q4; P5 Q4. Type levels and covers, distinguish maximal from greatest. |\n| Core | Recurrences | P2 Q6; P3 Q7; P5 Q6. Include homogeneous, repeated-root and non-homogeneous practice. |\n| Core | Graphs | Appears in all five papers: degree, isomorphism, reachability, Hamilton, planar, coloring, complement, counts. |\n| Core | MST | P1 Q7 (both algorithms); P4 Q9 (Kruskal). Steps, cycle/cut rule, total weight. |\n| Past-paper extras | Groups | P1 Q8; P2 Q8; P3 Q9; P5 Q7. Use associativity, identities, inverse and cancellation explicitly. |\n| Past-paper extras | Knights and knaves | P2 Q1; P4 Q1. Enumerate all consistent assignments; a spy is unconstrained. |\n| Past-paper extras | Counting / pigeonhole | P3 Q5; P4 Q5; P5 Q5. State boxes, overlap and minimum guarantee. |\n| Past-paper extras | Sets / functions / countability | P1 Q2-3; P4 Q3; P5 Q3. State domain/codomain and prove cardinality claims. |\n| Past-paper extras | Proofs / counterexamples | P1 Q1-2; P4 Q2; recurring throughout graphs and groups. Existence and uniqueness are separate. |\n| Extra | Remaining course material | Quantifier notation (P3 Q2), closure algorithms and other less-prioritised details. Review after core and past-paper extras. |\n\nA core label marks the professor\'s category, not a prediction of a specific question or a promised share for each category. The bank places knights/knaves in logic but marks them past.\n\n';
